01:32.500 --> 01:35.720
With the International Cup being hosted in Japan soon,

01:35.720 --> 01:39.990
we can't afford to lose this game, even if it is just a training game.

01:40.410 --> 01:44.480
Especially since the Dutch will bring their best players.

01:44.480 --> 01:48.840
Katagiri-kun, can we really take them on with all the young players?

01:48.840 --> 01:50.010
Yes.

01:50.010 --> 01:56.980
I firmly believe Ohzora Tsubasa, Hyuga Kojiro, and the others will change Japanese soccer.

01:57.470 --> 01:58.780
Very well.

01:58.780 --> 02:01.500
Do it your way if you're that confident about it.

02:02.270 --> 02:04.460
Thank you, Chairman.

02:04.460 --> 02:08.500
There is one more young player I would like to include on the team.

02:13.340 --> 02:15.630
The time has finally come.

02:15.630 --> 02:17.340
I've been dreaming about it!

02:22.600 --> 02:24.460
Are you ready, Aoi?

02:25.700 --> 02:26.650
Yes!

02:32.140 --> 02:37.260
<b>Aoi Shingo Takes the Stage!</b>

02:32.140 --> 02:37.260
<b>Aoi Shingo Takes the Stage!</b>

02:37.380 --> 02:42.020
J-Village, Fukushima Prefecture

02:39.610 --> 02:42.260
Gather around, everyone.

02:46.530 --> 02:48.740
Let me introduce you to a new player.

02:49.250 --> 02:53.700
This is Aoi Shingo. He'll be joining the camp starting today.

02:53.700 --> 02:58.700
He's playing for the Italian League's FC Lombardy.

02:58.700 --> 03:00.860
FC Lombardy?

03:00.860 --> 03:02.870
Aoi Shingo?

03:03.360 --> 03:04.740
I've never heard of this guy.

03:04.740 --> 03:08.120
A new star on the stage?

03:08.580 --> 03:10.220
Do you guys know him?

03:12.060 --> 03:14.220
Nice to meet you! I'm Aoi Shingo!

03:14.220 --> 03:18.200
It's awesome for an unknown player like me to be chosen to represent Japan!

03:18.200 --> 03:21.210
I'm not surprised none of you know my name.

03:21.210 --> 03:24.460
I've never played in any national tournaments,

03:25.170 --> 03:27.240
but I'll do my best!

03:27.240 --> 03:29.720
There's no stopping for a green light (ao shingou),

03:29.720 --> 03:32.040
and there's no stopping Aoi Shingo either!

03:32.040 --> 03:34.520
Once I start running, no one can stop me!

03:35.060 --> 03:36.620
Nice to meet you!

03:36.620 --> 03:38.190
What a weird guy.

03:38.190 --> 03:39.990
Just like you, Ishizaki!

03:39.990 --> 03:41.180
He's nothing like me!

03:43.470 --> 03:45.210
I'm Ohzora Tsubasa.

03:45.210 --> 03:45.940
Nice to meet you.

03:47.680 --> 03:49.380
Pleased to meet you!

03:49.380 --> 03:53.440
FC Lombardy is a Division II team.

03:53.440 --> 03:55.320
Tsubasa-kun, let's continue.

03:55.320 --> 03:57.900
Tell me about your experience playing soccer in Spain.

03:58.670 --> 04:00.900
How do you communicate with other players?

04:02.900 --> 04:06.360
Tsubasa-san sure is amazing!

04:06.860 --> 04:10.460
Wakabayashi-kun, it's halfway into the camp. How are you feeling?

04:10.460 --> 04:14.060
I'm moving well, and I think I'll be able to play a relaxed game.

04:14.060 --> 04:17.180
Looks like Coach Louvois thinks very highly of you.

04:17.180 --> 04:21.270
Please tell me about your plans for the game as "Japan's Godly Protector."

04:21.270 --> 04:25.340
I have the confidence to protect the goal against the Dutch.

04:25.340 --> 04:28.530
They've clinched the starting position.

04:28.530 --> 04:30.700
They're in a whole different league compared to us.

04:40.050 --> 04:41.170
Come in.

04:41.490 --> 04:42.860
Excuse me.

04:43.960 --> 04:48.020
Coach, I know I'm being rude, but there's something I want to know.

04:48.940 --> 04:50.060
What is it?

04:52.190 --> 04:57.870
Do you have any intention of making me the starting goalkeeper?

04:59.580 --> 05:03.380
I don't have overseas experience like Wakabayashi,

05:03.380 --> 05:07.730
but I don't think my skills are inferior compared to him.

05:07.730 --> 05:13.580
If it's already decided in your mind, then I would like you to tell me.

05:14.750 --> 05:21.030
Unfortunately, my plan for the Dutch game is pretty much set in stone.

05:21.030 --> 05:25.300
The starting goalkeeper will be... Wakabayashi Genzo.

05:25.300 --> 05:28.180
It's time for practice. Get going.

05:49.110 --> 05:50.820
What's up, Wakashimazu?

05:50.820 --> 05:54.900
There's no point waging a battle that's already lost.

05:55.490 --> 05:57.060
What are you talking about?

05:57.060 --> 06:01.100
The coach told me that Wakabayashi will be the starting goalkeeper.

06:02.420 --> 06:06.120
There's no point in me staying on this team.

06:07.740 --> 06:08.930
Wait!

06:08.930 --> 06:11.740
Don't give up if you like soccer!

06:14.260 --> 06:16.140
Uh, well...

06:16.140 --> 06:20.470
Think about it! Being nominated to represent Japan is amazing.

06:20.470 --> 06:22.020
Besides, it's not decided yet...

06:22.020 --> 06:24.260
What does some newcomer like you know?

06:24.260 --> 06:27.810
I've... I've always aimed to be number one.

06:27.810 --> 06:32.200
To become the starting goalkeeper for Japan!

06:33.990 --> 06:34.980
Wakashimazu...

06:34.980 --> 06:37.170
Wait! Wakashimazu!

06:45.600 --> 06:48.620
He took Hyuga's shot using only one hand!

06:58.120 --> 06:59.380
Wakashimazu-san!

07:01.420 --> 07:03.060
There's no point stopping him now.

07:03.510 --> 07:04.860
Wakashimazu will be just fine.

07:05.490 --> 07:06.330
Let's go!

07:10.200 --> 07:11.380
Tsubasa-san.

07:11.850 --> 07:15.160
This isn't the first time we met.

07:16.850 --> 07:19.620
11th Annual Soccer Festival



We Welcome The Nankatsu Soccer Team




Winner Of The National Championship

07:24.700 --> 07:26.340
NANKATSU FC                           NAKAHARA JR. HIGH

07:27.460 --> 07:29.260
Why are you crying, Shingo?

07:29.260 --> 07:31.600
Everyone knew we'd lose.

07:31.600 --> 07:32.620
Yeah, yeah!

07:32.620 --> 07:37.310
It was an honor just to get to play against Nankatsu, the reigning National Champions!

07:37.310 --> 07:38.610
I'll go and ask for hand shakes!

07:38.610 --> 07:39.260
Me, too!

07:41.320 --> 07:43.800
I'm sick of this team!

07:44.120 --> 07:46.460
I'll just quit soccer!

07:53.640 --> 07:56.060
You have some good techniques, Number 12.

07:56.060 --> 07:58.990
If you love soccer, then don't quit!

08:09.960 --> 08:10.880
Next!

08:10.880 --> 08:11.670
Yes!

08:14.910 --> 08:19.490
Those words from Tsubasa-san kept me from quitting soccer,

08:19.490 --> 08:22.420
and they inspired me to go to Italy on my own!

08:25.670 --> 08:27.020
That guy's not bad.

08:28.460 --> 08:31.940
Okay, get in teams of two and practice shooting.

08:32.380 --> 08:35.350
Wakabayashi and Morizaki, go cover each goal.

08:35.350 --> 08:37.130
Odd-numbered players practice on Wakabayashi's side.

08:37.130 --> 08:39.350
Even-numbered players on Morizaki's side.

08:39.350 --> 08:40.320
All right!

08:46.780 --> 08:47.810
There it is!

08:47.810 --> 08:49.380
Tsubasa-kun's Drive Shot!

08:49.820 --> 08:50.620
Next!

08:50.620 --> 08:52.000
Awesome!

08:52.000 --> 08:54.650
That's the real Drive Shot from Tsubasa-san!

08:54.650 --> 08:55.980
I gotta put on a show, too!

08:55.980 --> 09:00.370
Aoi Shingo. Let's see the shot you practiced in Italy.

09:00.370 --> 09:01.980
All right, come!

09:01.980 --> 09:03.050
Here I come!

09:08.390 --> 09:10.980
Whoa, that's a big home run!

09:14.580 --> 09:16.650
What's with that guy?

09:16.650 --> 09:19.650
Aren't chances things you make for yourself?

09:19.650 --> 09:20.660
Katagiri-san?

09:20.660 --> 09:25.560
Even if you're not the starting goalkeeper in the coach's plan,

09:25.560 --> 09:29.660
isn't it up to you whether or not you can create that chance?

09:30.710 --> 09:35.560
Do you know why Aoi Shingo, who's never made a name for himself, was chosen?

09:36.490 --> 09:38.900
You guys are elites.

09:38.900 --> 09:43.540
You've all played in national tourneys and have made it to the apex of Japanese soccer.

09:43.540 --> 09:46.460
But Shingo is different.

09:46.460 --> 09:50.300
He climbed up to where he is now from the ground up.

09:50.300 --> 09:53.810
That is, in no way, an easy path.

09:54.700 --> 09:57.180
Shingo left for Italy at the age of 15.

09:57.730 --> 10:04.180
A man he met in the airport said he could secure a chance for him to try out for FC Lombardy,

10:04.180 --> 10:06.740
but he ended up losing all his money to that scam artist.

10:10.730 --> 10:15.700
Wow! This is FC Lombardy's home ground?

10:16.170 --> 10:21.760
I can really try out for the team if I paid two million lire?

10:22.500 --> 10:24.220
Here you go.

10:25.540 --> 10:27.360
The coach will show up soon.

10:27.360 --> 10:29.500
I've already negotiated with him.

10:29.500 --> 10:30.220
See you.

10:35.740 --> 10:37.390
You must be the coach!

10:37.390 --> 10:40.770
I'm Aoi Shingo, and I'm here to try out for the team.

10:40.770 --> 10:42.580
Who told you that?

10:42.580 --> 10:45.660
We aren't having any tryouts for a while.

10:45.660 --> 10:46.260
Huh?

10:46.260 --> 10:49.280
No tryouts?

10:49.280 --> 10:50.260
B-But...

10:54.600 --> 10:55.740
Thank you.

10:58.430 --> 11:00.690
What do I do now?

11:00.690 --> 11:02.510
You can have this.

11:02.510 --> 11:03.490
Here.

11:03.940 --> 11:05.470
Thank you!

11:07.090 --> 11:09.580
We have to help each other when we're in need.

11:10.080 --> 11:11.380
Hey!

11:11.380 --> 11:12.570
Not good!

11:13.020 --> 11:14.300
Wait!

11:17.160 --> 11:18.510
Polish my shoes.

11:22.000 --> 11:22.900
Yes.

11:28.950 --> 11:30.420
Thank you.

11:32.510 --> 11:35.940
Where did that man go?

12:00.800 --> 12:01.850
Thank you!

12:02.920 --> 12:06.410
Since then, Shingo rented an apartment nearby,

12:06.410 --> 12:09.210
and made his living by polishing shoes and lifting balls.

12:09.750 --> 12:11.300
But one day...

12:11.300 --> 12:13.000
That's right...

12:13.000 --> 12:16.460
Why did I come here?

12:16.460 --> 12:20.580
Didn't I come here to play real soccer?

12:20.580 --> 12:23.950
What do I do from now on?

12:24.400 --> 12:25.410
What do I...

12:47.290 --> 12:51.390
Sir, can I help you polish those shoes?

12:51.390 --> 12:53.180
Who are you?

12:53.180 --> 12:57.400
I came from Japan to play real soccer.

12:57.400 --> 13:00.610
I really want to play soccer here,

13:00.610 --> 13:04.940
but I don't know anyone here. I don't know what to do.

13:04.940 --> 13:06.020
So...

13:06.020 --> 13:09.980
Please let me help you polish shoes as a start.

13:09.980 --> 13:13.180
That way, I may be able to get a foot in the door.

13:13.180 --> 13:16.180
Please, give me a chance!

13:17.960 --> 13:19.060
Stand up.

13:20.350 --> 13:21.060
Yes.

13:27.900 --> 13:31.140
You have nice legs.

13:32.140 --> 13:35.960
Nice legs for soccer.

13:42.500 --> 13:44.770
Perrini injured his ankle.

13:44.770 --> 13:46.780
He can't play in the practice game today.

13:46.780 --> 13:49.880
I guess that means you'll have to play.

13:49.880 --> 13:51.900
Hey, Coach!

13:51.900 --> 13:55.420
I have a spare player right here.

13:56.330 --> 13:59.240
Whether or not you can seize the chance is in your hands...

13:59.240 --> 14:01.140
No, in your legs.

14:02.010 --> 14:03.340
Sir...

14:04.240 --> 14:05.150
Yes!

14:07.120 --> 14:13.770
And so, Shingo got the chance to join FC Lombardy on his own.

14:14.400 --> 14:17.250
It seems he was picked on a lot,

14:17.250 --> 14:20.020
but he never gave up and improved his skills.

14:20.930 --> 14:25.380
The flexibility that comes from being optimistic about everything,

14:25.380 --> 14:27.330
the passion towards soccer,

14:27.330 --> 14:28.340
single-mindedness,

14:29.050 --> 14:33.440
and skills, every single one of these is required for players who represent Japan,

14:33.440 --> 14:34.640
Wakashimazu.

14:44.530 --> 14:46.380
Practicing your shooting?

14:46.910 --> 14:48.090
Wakashimazu-san!

14:48.090 --> 14:49.900
I'll stop them.

14:50.950 --> 14:51.910
Uh...

14:51.910 --> 14:53.860
Thank you.

14:58.590 --> 15:00.710
What are you watching, Tsubasa?

15:02.010 --> 15:03.300
Wakashimazu.

15:03.300 --> 15:04.140
Aoi!

15:08.860 --> 15:13.640
He must have practiced on his own everyday in Italy, too.

15:14.040 --> 15:15.780
I've heard from Katagiri-san

15:15.780 --> 15:19.540
that he practices by himself - two or three times more than anyone else.

15:19.540 --> 15:23.280
I can tell how much he loves soccer just from looking into his eyes.

15:23.280 --> 15:25.780
I was like that when I was little, too.

15:25.780 --> 15:29.930
He's really something, to head to Italy all by himself.

15:29.930 --> 15:34.220
I can see why Aoi was chosen as a candidate.

15:34.220 --> 15:37.380
We can't let him leave us behind.

15:40.100 --> 15:42.100
Hey, you'll catch cold.

15:46.130 --> 15:47.710
W-What's this?

15:50.280 --> 15:53.620
An Aoi Shingo original muscle-strengthening jacket.

15:53.620 --> 15:55.800
I'm small, right?

15:55.800 --> 15:59.260
So I thought I'd cover for that handicap by building up strength.

16:06.550 --> 16:10.760
I can't become Tsubasa-san no matter how hard I try,

16:10.760 --> 16:18.600
but I believe there must be something I can do as a member of the Japanese team.

16:21.940 --> 16:23.100
What is that?

16:23.100 --> 16:26.540
This? It's my good luck charm.

16:38.450 --> 16:40.020
Ohzora Tsubasa-san!

16:41.720 --> 16:46.260
Tsubasa-san, I wish you good luck playing soccer in Brazil!

16:49.880 --> 16:52.020
Number 12 of Nakahara Jr. High!

16:58.500 --> 17:00.220
It's a Brazilian coin.

17:00.220 --> 17:02.060
Good luck to you, too!

17:06.690 --> 17:09.640
Tsubasa-san, I'll do my best.

17:09.640 --> 17:12.010
I'll never give up.

17:19.300 --> 17:24.650
Actually, there was something I wanted to tell him at the airport,

17:24.650 --> 17:26.260
but I couldn't say it.

17:29.010 --> 17:31.940
All right! I'll play hard again today!

17:34.670 --> 17:36.430
I'm first!

17:36.430 --> 17:37.830
H-Huh?

17:43.320 --> 17:45.900
Too bad, I was first to show up.

17:48.540 --> 17:50.940
Wakashimazu-san, good morning!

17:51.660 --> 17:52.900
Good morning.

18:01.660 --> 18:02.590
Good morning.

18:02.590 --> 18:03.500
Yo!

18:06.870 --> 18:08.580
Head Coach. Coach.

18:09.730 --> 18:12.820
I'm sorry for skipping practice yesterday.

18:15.210 --> 18:16.920
Let's begin practice!

18:16.920 --> 18:17.660
Yes!

18:19.740 --> 18:23.090
You will divide into two teams today and have a practice game.

18:23.090 --> 18:26.660
Put on your vests and get to your position.

18:26.660 --> 18:32.580
Man, this brings back memories! All of us from the Nankatsu team are here!

18:32.580 --> 18:35.100
It reminds me of the national tournament!

18:36.000 --> 18:37.100
All right, let's go!

18:38.750 --> 18:40.590
It's just like back then.

18:41.170 --> 18:46.280
That one time I played against Tsubasa-san.

18:45.740 --> 18:48.180
NANKATSU FC                           NAKAHARA JR. HIGH

18:55.430 --> 18:58.540
All right, I'll score a goal this time!

19:01.980 --> 19:04.060
He's really fired up.

19:04.060 --> 19:06.220
Don't worry, I'll stop him!

19:10.300 --> 19:12.040
He's fast!

19:12.040 --> 19:14.020
It's really true. He can't be stopped!

19:14.020 --> 19:15.530
Aoi Shingo...

19:15.530 --> 19:18.180
Looks like he's a player we can use creatively.

19:18.180 --> 19:19.300
Yeah.

19:38.470 --> 19:40.990
I still have a long way to go!

19:40.990 --> 19:43.020
I see your technique is still good,

19:43.020 --> 19:44.640
Number 12 of Nakahara Jr. High.

19:45.300 --> 19:47.890
You remembered me, Tsubasa-san?

19:48.420 --> 19:52.020
You also came to see me off when I left for Brazil, right?

19:52.020 --> 19:54.060
Tsubasa-san...

19:54.060 --> 19:59.440
There's something I couldn't tell you at the airport.

19:59.440 --> 20:01.490
But I can now.

20:01.490 --> 20:07.830
I'll definitely participate in the International Cup to represent Japan with you, Tsubasa-san.

20:07.830 --> 20:10.420
And fight to be number one in the world!

20:10.420 --> 20:12.940
Good. Let's do our best!

20:12.940 --> 20:14.540
Yes!

20:18.850 --> 20:24.980
We will now announce the Japanese players for the training game against the Netherlands.

20:37.250 --> 20:39.380
Oh! Willem and Gustaf are both here!

20:39.380 --> 20:42.750
This is the lineup soccer fans wanted to see!

20:42.750 --> 20:50.100
Yeah, who'd have predicted that the top-notch Dutch team would be eliminated so early?

20:50.100 --> 20:53.210
It just means that there's no guarantee in soccer.

20:53.210 --> 20:57.130
Does that mean Japan has a chance to win?

20:58.260 --> 21:02.820
International Stadium, Yokohama

21:14.880 --> 21:18.330
Good Luck, Japan!

21:18.330 --> 21:21.340
Note: The flag on the right has written "Ohzora Tsubasa" on it.

21:21.340 --> 21:24.020
I've been waiting, Tsubasa!

21:24.020 --> 21:28.970
I can't wait to see Tsubasa-kun in action after all his training in Brazil!

21:28.970 --> 21:32.660
Let's see the techniques Roberto taught him!

21:34.940 --> 21:39.420
It's been four years since we were able to see Tsubasa-kun play soccer in a stadium.

21:39.420 --> 21:41.940
Good luck, Tsubasa-kun!

21:41.940 --> 21:54.850
Japan! Japan! Japan!

22:04.020 --> 22:10.020
Preview

22:05.780 --> 22:09.630
It's the training game against the Dutch team, filled with their best players.

22:09.630 --> 22:12.700
The stadium was painted blue by 70,000 fans.

22:12.700 --> 22:18.670
And so, the Dutch "Total Football" strikes!

22:18.670 --> 22:20.220
Don't lose, everyone!

22:20.220 --> 22:23.120
Score a goal no matter who you're up against!

